<title>FINLAND: Finnish Dec EU-harmonised CPI rises 1.5 pct - SF.</title>
<headline>Finnish Dec EU-harmonised CPI rises 1.5 pct - SF.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Finnish consumer price index partially harmonised to European Union standards rose 1.5 percent year-on-year in December after a 1.4 percent rise in November, Statistics Finland (SF) said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>				Dec 1996	Nov 1996    Dec 1995</p>
<p> Yr/Yr			+1.5 pct	 +1.4 pct   +0.4 pct</p>
<p> Mth/Mth		     0.0 pct	 -0.1 pct   -0.1 pct</p>
<p> Index (base 1994=100)   102.4	    102.3	100.83</p>
<p>According to SF's regular national method of calculation, Finnish consumer prices were unchanged month-on-month in December and they rose 0.8 percent year-on-year, it said.</p>
<p>			     Dec 1996	 Nov 1996     Dec 1995</p>
<p> Yr/yr		     +0.8 pct	  +0.7 pct	+0.3 pct</p>
<p> Mth/mth		 -/+0.0 pct	  -0.3 pct	-0.1 pct</p>
<p> Index (base 1990=100)  112.7	     112.7	   111.8</p>
<p>Five economists' average forecast for the national CPI figure was for a 0.8 percent rise year-on-year and a zero percent rise month-on-month.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki Newsroom +358 - 9 - 680 50 245</p>
</text>
